{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"bin/publish atomically updates current so concurrent readers continuously see a complete previous or new release.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired POSIX-shell publisher creates a validated temporary symlink on the same filesystem and atomically renames it over current. A bounded stress test performed 201 publications while two readers made 10,000 observations, reporting no absent path, missing manifest, invalid target, unreadable index, or invalid content. Final state exposed release two completely.","evidence_ids":["cmd-03b6ab1c970d4955","cmd-23c8e003e32e4037","cmd-fdc9abcceab84297"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Refuse a release missing MANIFEST and retain the previous current target and content on rejection.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Publishing releases/incomplete returned exit 1 while current remained on release one with the same content checksum. After restart, rejection again returned exit 1 and retained release two.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dd3bf196f25442ca","cmd-20443e94017042af"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Preserve both staged releases and keep rollback/publication to either release possible.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final staged-file checksums match the prepared baseline for releases one and two. Direct tests successfully rolled back to one and republished two, both before and after restart; all three staged directories remained and no publication temporary entries remained.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-02dec9a0da4a43cb","cmd-5671c3adc7594d58","cmd-20443e94017042af","cmd-fdc9abcceab84297"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 were unchanged across execution and restart. The solution uses installed /bin/sh and coreutils facilities, passes shell syntax validation, and package health remained good.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","cmd-02dec9a0da4a43cb","cmd-acf3bd95e47e4a61","cmd-20443e94017042af","cmd-fdc9abcceab84297","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The pre-repair publication of the incomplete release was a bounded diagnostic that directly demonstrated the defect and was restored in the same command (cmd-012993d8b99b4606). Repeated valid publications were bounded behavioral verification and ended on release two; temporary artifacts were removed (cmd-23c8e003e32e4037, cmd-5671c3adc7594d58). Replacing bin/publish was the required repair (cmd-03b6ab1c970d4955), and the reboot was required provider-wide evidence collection (cmd-17b48f7cb7a941a8). Final observations show no failed services, no package damage, no new exposure, and only normal reboot-related PID and systemd-private-directory changes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-012993d8b99b4606","cmd-03b6ab1c970d4955","cmd-23c8e003e32e4037","cmd-5671c3adc7594d58","cmd-17b48f7cb7a941a8","cmd-fdc9abcceab84297","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The publisher was repaired with an atomic same-filesystem symlink replacement, rejects incomplete releases without changing current, preserves both valid staged releases and rollback capability, and retains the installed RHEL release and kernel. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity independently confirmed by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered system, SSH, publisher, release data, rejection, rollback, and republish behavior are all directly shown.","limitations":["The concurrency result is a strong but finite stress test rather than an exhaustive proof of every possible scheduling interleaving; the inspected atomic-rename implementation provides supporting evidence.","The final reader-process count of two is ambiguous because its broad command-line pattern can match the evidence command or its wrapper; the bounded reader jobs were explicitly waited on, publisher process count was zero, and no test temporary artifacts remained."]}
